Mac Catalyst: return to UIKit between game frames.

The UIKit shell schedules mainLoop on the main thread after mainProc finishes
initialization. Catalyst uses AppKit event dispatch, which a nested Foundation
run loop does not drive. Each callback runs one solo or net frame and returns;
stage setup and teardown continue through the existing code on the next call.
iOS, visionOS and the desktop reference retain their existing blocking loop.

--- a/port/src/pdmain.c
+++ b/port/src/pdmain.c
@@ -325,9 +325,17 @@
 	// test aids: a mod's audio entered after the boot's banks (modaudio.c)
 	modAudioTestSwitches();
 
+#if defined(PLATFORM_IOS) && TARGET_OS_MACCATALYST
+	// Catalyst dispatches input through AppKit's outer event loop. The shell
+	// calls one frame at a time on the main thread, returning to UIKit between
+	// frames instead of nesting CFRunLoop inside an infinite game loop.
+	extern void pdMacScheduleFrames(void (*frame)(void));
+	pdMacScheduleFrames(mainLoop);
+#else
 	while (true) {
 		mainLoop();
 	}
+#endif
 }
 
